-- title:
--   Level-M/p diamond acts on the pole chart as Specσ
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a natural number $M$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbf Z/M)^\times$, and assume $M$ and $M/p$ are nonzero. Assume further that the Laurent series $j$-invariant `jqModC ℚ` lies in the $q$-expansion field $\mathbf Q$-intermediate field `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbf Z)$, and let $\mathfrak X$ be a structure `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, a package of integral-model data for $X_H(M)$ over the ring `R p` together with the auxiliary level-$(M/p)$ model, its forgetful morphism and its diamond isomorphisms. Let $e \in (\mathbf Z/(M/p))^\times$, and let $\sigma$ be an `R p`-algebra automorphism of the pole-chart algebra `chartAlgInf p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj`, i.e. of the subalgebra of elements of `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓN p M H hpM)` integral over the `R p`-subalgebra generated by $(\mathrm{jAt})^{-1}$. The hypothesis on $\sigma$ is that it reads on $q$-expansions as the inverse diamond: for every $b$ in that chart algebra, the coefficientwise extension `coeffEmb` to $\overline{\mathbf Q}((q))$ of the Laurent series of $\sigma b$ equals the image of the Laurent series of $b$ under the inverse of `diamondAutHBar (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM) e`, the diamond automorphism of `xHFunctionFieldBar (M / p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` attached to $e$, where `infSubgroup p M H hpM` is the image of $H$ under the reduction $(\mathbf Z/M)^\times \to (\mathbf Z/(M/p))^\times$. The conclusion is the commuting square $\iota_\infty$ followed by $(\mathfrak X.\mathrm{dia0}\ e).\mathrm{hom}$ equals $\operatorname{Spec}(\sigma)$ followed by $\iota_\infty$, where $\iota_\infty =$ `ιInf p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj` is the pole chart of the two-chart integral model at level `ΓN p M H hpM`.
--
--   This identifies the level-$(M/p)$ diamond operator of the integral model on the pole chart (the chart at $j = \infty$) with the spectrum of the chart automorphism whose effect on $q$-expansions is the inverse diamond; it is the level-$(M/p)$ counterpart of the corresponding statement at level $\Gamma_H(M)$. It is used in the analysis of the diamond action on the charts, and is cited by the companion statement for the finite chart.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XHDRModelAtP_iotaInf_comp_dia0_hom_eq_spec_map_comp_iotaInf.lean

